# Worksheet text

When building a homework sheet:

- Do not write a grammar description. Leave it empty. If a description has to be there, the only text is `coming soon`.
- Do not add instructions that explain the grammar.
- The line under a blank is the English meaning, with no parentheses.
- Use JD's glass-card definition when that word already has one. Do not rewrite his wording. If there is no card, use a short English gloss and say which words had no card.
